@startuml st2i_organigramme
title Functional organisation of ST2i

' Organisation by activity line, as the company presents it publicly. The chart
' deliberately stops at the department level: ST2i staffs its technical teams
' per project from a shared pool of geomatics experts, developers and
' technicians, so below this level there is no fixed hierarchy to draw.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ArrowThickness 1
skinparam TitleFontName  Helvetica
skinparam TitleFontSize  13
skinparam TitleFontColor #333333
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor     #808080
  BorderThickness 1
  FontColor       #333333
  FontName        Helvetica
  FontSize        11
}
skinparam noteBorderColor     #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam noteFontName        Helvetica
skinparam noteFontSize        9

rectangle "STUDI Group" as GROUP #F7F7F7
rectangle "ST2i\nGeneral management" as DG

rectangle "Studies\nand consulting" as ETU
rectangle "Development and\nintegration of solutions" as DEV
rectangle "Geomatics" as GEO
rectangle "Project-owner\nassistance" as AMO
rectangle "Distribution of\ntechnical software" as DIS

rectangle "Multidisciplinary technical teams\n(geomatics experts, developers, technicians)" as TEAMS #F7F7F7

GROUP -- DG

DG -- ETU
DG -- DEV
DG -- GEO
DG -- AMO
DG -- DIS

ETU .. TEAMS
DEV .. TEAMS
GEO .. TEAMS
AMO .. TEAMS
DIS .. TEAMS

note bottom of TEAMS
  Teams are assembled per project across the activity lines.
  Steering the workload of one person across several simultaneous
  projects is exactly the problem this platform addresses.
end note

note right of DEV
  The activity line this project belongs to,
  and whose economics the platform steers.
end note

@enduml
